I am walking around the Sunday market.
I stop in front of a stall of old things.
There are many different and old things here.
Many years ago, people used these things.
An elderly man is sitting in the stall.
"Namaste Kaka," I say to him.
I point at a small brass bell nearby.
"How much is this bell for?" I ask.
"This is for two hundred rupees, Madam," he says.
Then I look at the top shelf.
There is a carved wooden box there.
"And how much is that box for?"
"That box is very old."
"That is for five hundred rupees," he tells me.
There are also some old coins on the table.
"From when are these coins?" I ask.
"Those coins are from fifty years ago," Kaka says proudly.
I smile and thank him.
I do not buy anything.
But I really like looking at these old things.
I walk ahead smiling.
